===Etymology 3===
A variant of {{m|en|screed}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|screes|screeing|screed}}

# To [[flatten]] or [[level#Verb|level]] [[concrete#Noun|concrete]] while still [[wet#Adjective|wet]], and [[remove#Verb|remove]] [[protruding#Adjective|protruding]] [[gravel]] and [[stone#Noun|stones]] from the surface.
#* {{quote-book|author=United States Tennessee Valley Authority|title=Concrete Production and Control: Tennessee Valley Authority Projects|series=Technical Report (Tennessee Valley Authority)|seriesvolume=no. 21|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Government Publishing Office|Government Printing Office]]|year=1948|page=44|oclc=33380611|passage=The crushing and '''screeing''' equipment owned by the TVA was transferred from job to job, and the availability of this equipment was one of the factors in determining who would produce the aggregate.}}
#* {{quote-journal|title=For the Dogs|editor=Duane Raver|magazine=Wildlife in North Carolina|location=Raleigh, N.C.|publisher={{w|North Carolina Wildlife Resources Commission}}|month=September|year=1974|volume=XXXVIII|issue=9|page=8|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/wildlifeinnorthc38nort#page/n237/mode/1up/|issn=0043-549X|oclc=2401003|passage=Sequence of Construction&nbsp;– Circular Dog Kennel. {{...}} Pour concrete. Use a straight 1-inch pipe about 12 feet long to '''scree''' each section. Extra help should be on hand to get '''screeing''' done. {{...}} Specify a concrete mix that will not harden before '''screeing''' can be completed; do not order more concrete than can be property '''screed''' at one time; {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Maxine Kumin|chapter=VII|title=Quit Monks or Die!: A Novel|location=Ashland, Or.|publisher=Story Line Press|year=1999|page=44|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/quitmonksordieno00kumi#page/44/mode/1up/|isbn=978-1-885266-77-4|passage=He was a stupid sonofabitch who didn't '''scree''' the concrete enough, his corner post was an eighth of an inch out of plumb, and what asshole set these louvers upside down?}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Theodore Osmundson|title=Roof Gardens: History, Design, and Construction|location=New York, N.Y.; London|publisher={{w|W. W. Norton & Company}}|year=1999|page=196|isbn=978-0-393-73012-8|passage=The sand bed is '''screed''' in preparation for laying the precast paving.}}

